{"nodes": [{"id": "sync", "label": "Shopify Data Sync", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "sync_job", "label": "o_sync_job", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One active job per shop, enforced by a unique index. Status moves from queued to succeeded, partial, or failed."}, {"id": "sync_queue", "label": "sync.shop Queue", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "pg-boss queue. Policy exclusive, singletonKey is the shop id. The api enqueues after createSyncJob."}, {"id": "sync_run", "label": "runSync", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Products, then orders whose processed_at is within the last 90 days. One transaction per page upserts rows and saves the resume cursor and progress counters. One page of 25 orders is in memory at a time."}, {"id": "sync_tables", "label": "Synced Shopify Tables", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "t_product, t_product_variant, t_order, t_order_line_item, t_refund, t_refund_line_item, t_order_transaction, and o_sync_job. All carry tenant_id and shop_id, a composite foreign key to m_shop, forced RLS, and UNIQUE(shop_id, shopify_id). No customer personal data is stored. Money is NUMERIC(19,4) in shop currency."}, {"id": "sync_idempotent", "label": "Sync Page Idempotency", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "INSERT ON CONFLICT (shop_id, shopify_id) DO UPDATE. Replaying a page changes nothing. Duplicates inside one batch are collapsed and the newest wins."}, {"id": "sync_stale", "label": "No Rollback to Older Shopify Data", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Update only where the incoming shopify_updated_at is at least the stored value. A stale order is skipped together with its children. Line items missing from a new copy are deleted unless Shopify said the list was truncated."}, {"id": "sync_resume", "label": "Resumable Sync", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cursor and counters are written in the same transaction as each page. A retry restarts at the last committed page. pg-boss returns jobs of crashed workers after expireInSeconds. Five retries with a 30 second base and exponential backoff. 401 or 403 is not retried: the job fails and the shop is flagged reauth_required."}, {"id": "sync_throttle", "label": "Cost-aware Shopify Client", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sleeps using throttleStatus before the bucket empties, and retries THROTTLED, 429 using Retry-After, and 5xx with backoff."}, {"id": "sync_graphql", "label": "Paginated GraphQL", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Chosen instead of bulk operations for now. Seeded history is 150 orders; paging 25 orders per request streams in constant memory and is resumable. For stores with tens of thousands of orders, add a bulk-operation source behind the same runSync stages. Nested refund line items need care in bulk JSONL."}, {"id": "sync_refund_date", "label": "Refund Effective Date", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The profit engine must use t_refund.processed_at. The REFUND transaction timestamp is the creation time and can be months later. Cancelling an unpaid order creates a refund with line items but 0.00 money and must not count as a monetary refund."}, {"id": "sync_null_unknown", "label": "NULL Means Unknown", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "fee_amount NULL means Shopify reports no fee data, never zero. t_product_variant.unit_cost_amount NULL means no cost is set. Orders keep processed_at as the business date; shopify_created_at is only the import time for backdated orders."}, {"id": "sync_discounts", "label": "Use Shopify Discount Amounts", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Shopify rounds percentage discounts slightly differently from a per-line calculation. Always use the amounts Shopify reports; never recompute discounts. t_order.subtotal_amount is after discounts and before shipping."}, {"id": "sync_read_all_orders", "label": "read_all_orders History Limit", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Orders older than 60 days need the read_all_orders scope for real merchants. Seeded orders have createdAt equal to now, so the dev store does not exercise that limit."}, {"id": "sync_webhooks", "label": "Webhooks and Privacy Handling", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Live updates, the nightly reconcile, and uninstall and privacy handling are described in webhooks.md. A re-sync re-imports the 90 day window idempotently."}, {"id": "sync_pg_boss", "label": "pg-boss", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "sync_tables", "target": "database_m_shop", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "sync_tables", "target": "database_rls", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "profit_engine_decimal", "target": "sync_tables", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "sync_refund_date", "target": "profit_engine_package", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "sync_null_unknown", "target": "profit_engine_missing", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "sync_discounts", "target": "profitability_allocation", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "sync", "target": "sync_job", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "sync", "target": "sync_queue", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "sync_queue", "target": "sync_pg_boss", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "sync_queue", "target": "sync_job", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "sync_queue", "target": "sync_run", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "sync_run", "target": "sync_tables", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "sync_idempotent", "target": "sync_run", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "sync_stale", "target": "sync_run", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "sync_resume", "target": "sync_run", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/sync.md", 